  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ダッタンソバ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%80%E3%83%83%E3%82%BF%E3%83%B3%E3%82%BD%E3%83%90",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 109851501,
      "text": "ダッタンソバ は、タデ科ソバ属の一年草。製粉・製麺して、蕎麦のように食用とされる。独特な強い苦みがあるため苦蕎麦（にがそば）とも呼ばれる。「ダッタン」は漢字で「韃靼」と書き、モンゴルに住む遊牧民族の古い呼び名のひとつであるタタール人のことである。ダッタンソバの食品名は、彼らが好んだことにちなんで名づけられたとされる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Fagopyrum tataricum",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fagopyrum_tataricum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1342296929,
      "text": "Fagopyrum tataricum, also known as Tartary buckwheat, green buckwheat, ku qiao, Tatar buckwheat, or bitter buckwheat, is a domesticated food plant in the genus Fagopyrum in the family Polygonaceae. With another species in the same genus, common buckwheat, it is often counted as a cereal, but the buckwheats are not closely related to true cereals."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Fagopyrum tataricum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fagopyrum_tataricum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 171582170,
      "text": "Fagopyrum tataricum es una especie de planta perteneciente a la familia Polygonaceae. Con otra especie del mismo género, el alforfón común, a menudo se considera como un cereal, pero a diferencia de los verdaderos cereales, no son gramíneas. Es decir que no se relacionan con el trigo."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Sarrasin de Tartarie",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarrasin_de_Tartarie",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 205563689,
      "text": "Le sarrasin de Tartarie ou « blé » noir fourrager est une plante de la famille des Polygonaceae."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Fagopyrum tataricum § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fagopyrum_tataricum#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1342296929,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Known in Chinese as \"bitter buckwheat\" (Chinese: 苦荞麦; pinyin: kǔqiáomài) and in Japan as dattan-soba (韃靼蕎麦/ダッタンソバ; 'Tartary buckwheat'), the plant was domesticated as a crop in East Asia and is also being cultivated in Europe and North America. While it is an unfamiliar food in the West, it is common in the Himalayan region today, as well as other regions in Southwest China such as Sichuan province. Tartary buckwheat is commonly roasted to make buckwheat tea, and it can also be distilled to make alcohol. While not traditionally eaten in Japan, due to its high rutin content it was briefly popular as a health fad in Japan in the late 1990s.\nThe plant has been cultivated in many parts of the world; however, when found among other crops it is considered a weed.  Less bitter varieties are now commercially available.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
